Local cinematic implementation in progress: srep-0000-cinematic-impact.md
introduces document version 1.3. The current patch adds bounded SRVOL/OpenVDB volume
assets, numbered cache sequences and integrity-pinned SRVSEQ render bakes,
explicit velocity-driven midpoint interpolation (advect and velocityGridX/Y/Z),
object3D volume instances, medium shading with temperature emission, native pyro
sources/impulses, scoped moving colliders and force fields, and
native particles3D emission, appearance and rigid collider references, and
ocean surfaces, image/mesh bathymetry, procedural swell, timed water impulses,
bounded native foam/spray tracers, and globe elevation shared by rendering and
rigid-body, particle and pyro colliders with explicit physical scale and DEM budgets,
and numbered mesh-sequence rendering with explicit interpolation/missing-frame policies.
The local rules are V8/VOL1-VOL9/PYRO1-PYRO8/P3D1-P3D6/OCN1-OCN5/GEO1-GEO3/MSQ1-MSQ4.
The remaining proposal surface is tracked in tools/evidence/cinematic-impact.json;
this is not an accepted upstream schema release.

